# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Lightweight "caption" translations for the persistent app shell (the
sidebar and top navbar rendered by templates/base.html).

This is a separate dictionary from the deep, page-by-page bilingual
English/Arabic content that's hardcoded throughout the other ~80 templates
(via `{% if current_locale == 'ar' %}...{% else %}...{% endif %}`), but it
is gated the exact same way: app.py's inject_globals() only ever passes
`t()` the resolved `current_locale`, which is English unless the user's
selected dashboard language IS the Owner's configured "Second Language".
So a field only ever shows translated text -- caption or deep content --
when that condition holds; picking any other language leaves everything
in English. Translation, when it does apply, is always English -> the
configured Second Language. A language/key with no entry falls back to
English.
"""

